      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transposition or total-daily-dose mix-up. Possible intended orders include:\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals, or 500 mg PO three times daily if you want a lower dose.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nWhich of these do you want? If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose."
      }
     ],
