      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as ORD-0001: metformin 1700 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals.\n\nThe order note says the total is 5,100 mg/day, which is above the usual maximum. It also says you confirmed the dose was intentional, on the specialist's recommendation, and that it's documented in the chart.\n\nBecause the dose is so high, you may want to monitor the patient closely. That could include renal function, lactate if symptoms develop, and GI tolerance. Pharmacy may also call to verify the order."
